  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a user, I want to choose my theme in a **Thème sub-menu with a live preview** of each theme, so that I see what I pick before I leave the screen. The **Legacy** theme keeps its accent hue slider; the other themes have fixed colours and no slider.\n\n### On hold\n\nHeld by the M5_OPEN decision: M5 opens after the M4 parity is validated, and the orchestrator opens it (operator decisions of 2026-11-02 on #379). ([decision](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/issues/379#issuecomment-6573879240))\n\n\n### Scope\n\nRevised by the operator on 2026-11-11 (replaces the 2026-10-28 \"10 presets on the slider\" scope). Contract: `docs/THEMES.md` §1–§3.\n\n- **Two kinds of theme.**\n  - **Legacy** (today's app): keeps the continuous « Teinte d'accent » hue slider and its stored keys (`theme_day_color_action`, `theme_night_color_action`), shape unchanged (LOT-121).\n  - **Themes with fixed colours** (those of the M4/M5 theme lots: Swift, Rétro 5250, OG clair and gris, Noël, Spooktober…): their accent comes from `theme.json`, **no slider is shown** for them.\n- **Theme selection sub-menu with a preview.** « Thème » opens a sub-screen, built like the app-icon picker (LOT-123, LOT-189: grouped, one tile per choice, check mark on the active one), where each theme tile shows a preview in light and dark (list row with the accent glyph, a link, a toggle, a badge). The preview updates as the slider moves, when Legacy is the highlighted theme. Choosing a fixed theme hides the slider; choosing Legacy shows it with the stored hue.\n- **Readable accent text** (decision 14, intentional difference from legacy): the raw tint stays for fills and toggles; text and glyphs drawn in the accent use a derived colour of the same hue that reaches 4.5:1 on the surface (the night tint is 3.5:1 on black at 240°). Applies to the Legacy slider; a fixed theme's accent is checked by LOT-188's contrast test. Rule in `docs/THEMES.md` §3.\n- **Open for the operator**: the 10 preset dots of the 2026-10-28 scope (hues Rouge 0.00 … Rose 0.92) are **dropped from this scope** unless you want them on the Legacy slider only; say so on this issue.\n- **Relation to LOT-188 (#729).** #729 owns the theme engine (`theme.json`, tokens, contrast test) and its gallery inline in « Thème ». This lot **depends on it** and turns that gallery into the sub-menu with a preview; whoever takes it adjusts #729's « Gallery » bullet by a comment, not a second gallery. Scope kept from the split of LOT-122 (#213): LOT-121 keeps the slider and its tints, LOT-122 the dark styles.\n\n- Module: App · Difficulty: medium · Priority: low · **M4** (operator 2026-11-07)\n- GAP ids: 145, 146. UXD: UXD-22. Spec: `docs/lots/LOT-180-accent.md` (to write).\n\n### Legacy counterpart\n\n`HFRswift/Swift/AppSettingsView.swift:326-333` (`applyTintHue`: day S0.65 B1.0, night S0.70 B0.95) and `:439-445` (« Teinte d'accent » slider) @ 87fe0d1c. The theme sub-menu with previews, the fixed-colour themes without a slider and the derived text colour are new.\n\n### Depends on\n\n- LOT-122 (#213, done)\n- **LOT-188 (#729, theme engine and gallery): open. Blocks this lot.**\n\n### Model\n\nSonnet → Opus (AGENTS.md §6)\n\n### Captures needed\n\n- none.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] An optional evolution: with Legacy selected and the slider untouched, colours and stored values are exactly LOT-121's.\n- [ ] Legacy theme: the slider still writes both accents in the legacy shape (any hue); a fixed-colour theme shows no slider and writes no accent key.\n- [ ] The Thème sub-menu shows a light and dark preview per theme; moving the slider updates the Legacy preview live.\n- [ ] Contrast test: the derived accent text ≥ 4.5:1 on every surface of light, dark Standard, Plus sombre and Noir OLED, for hues 0…1 in 0.01 steps.\n- [ ] The spec has its \"Legacy counterpart\" and \"UX evolutions\" sections.\n- [ ] View logic in `@Observable @MainActor` models tested with Swift Testing; each new test shown to fail without the change; `xcodebuild build test` green on iPhone 18 Pro and an iPad simulator (iOS 27.0); UI strings in French; light, dark and Dynamic Type XL checked; no new dependency.\n- [ ] This PR moves the LOT-180 row of `docs/LOTS.md` out of the M5 table and regenerates `tooling/roadmap/lots.json` and `milestones.json` (operator 2026-11-07 comment).\n\n### Before you start (agents and humans)\n\nRead, in order: AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, docs/agents/ORCHESTRATION.md, docs/agents/REVIEW-ROUNDS.md, docs/agents/LESSONS.md, docs/THEMES.md §1–§3, docs/ICONS.md (the picker pattern), the LOT-121 and LOT-122 specs. Claim with `/claim <session-id>`; PR body `LOT-180`, `Closes #420`, `Refs #154`, `Claim: <session-id>`.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
